  "body": "This question was raised in [bug 1221416](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1221416) when implementing `<details>` and `<summary>` elements in Firefox. \r\n\r\nThe spec does not specify how to customize of the triangle or should it be customizable, but we should support it somehow. The spec might need to clarify on this.\r\n\r\nCurrently, webkit supports a non-standard pseudo-class `summary::-webkit-details-marker` as [this article](http://blog.teamtreehouse.com/use-details-summary-elements) said.\r\n\r\n@upsuper proposed we could add `::marker` support for `<summary>` element in [pseudo-element spec](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-pseudo-4/#marker-pseudo). This makes sense to me.\r\n\r\nAny other ideas? @bzbarsky \r\n",
